1:["$","$Le",null,{"record":{"slug":"diverse-foods","section":"projects","title":["大食物馆：策划与在地实践","The Food Pavilion: design and fieldwork"],"date":"2023 —","status":["在地实践","Field practice"],"summary":["以食物连接生态、生产与生活。在屏南四坪村，老宅改造、内容研究与地方共创，共同构成大食物馆的实践。","Food connects ecology, production and everyday life. In Siping, an adapted historic house brings spatial design, research and local collaboration together."],"image":"/assets/food-museum.jpg","caption":["大食物馆现场与研究资料，乡土国际汇报 PDF 第6页。","Food Pavilion and research material. Countryside International presentation, p.6."],"topic":true,"chapters":[{"title":["2023—2024 / 从策划到开放","2023–2024 / From research to opening"],"text":["团队于2023年开始介入策划设计，自2024年起与屏南乡村振兴研究院合作开展项目。大食物馆于2024年5月24日正式开放。","The team began planning and design in 2023, collaborating with the Pingnan Rural Revitalization Research Institute from 2024. The pavilion opened on 24 May 2024."]},{"title":["在老宅中工作","Working with an existing house"],"text":["展馆由潘国老的祖宅改建。团队结合密集立柱、天井与院落的原有条件，以“抱柱桌”“挂梁柜”等展陈方式介入空间，组织食物、地方知识与生活经验。","Adapted from Pan Guolao’s ancestral home, the pavilion works with its dense timber columns and courtyards. Displays wrap around columns and hang from beams, bringing food and local knowledge into the existing structure."]},{"title":["从村庄到更广阔的交流","Beyond the pavilion"],"text":["村落走访、人物肖像与食物研究随后转化为“以食为天”的参展与传播内容。大食物馆也承载了2025国际会议的部分议程，并成为研习营的实践基础。","Village visits, portraits and food research informed the Food Ecology exhibition and media. The pavilion hosted sessions of the 2025 conference and provided a foundation for the study camp."]}],"related":["food-ecology","milan-food","camp-2025","conference-2025"],"sources":["milan","award"],"credits":["总策划：姜珺。创建单位包括中国美术学院视觉传播学院、屏南乡村振兴研究院及当地相关单位；完整团队署名见原文。","Lead planner: Jiang Jun. Founding partners include the School of Communication Design, CAA, the Pingnan Rural Revitalization Research Institute and local organizations. Full credits in the source articles."]}}]
